   "details": "grey horned helmet with nasal guard, brim and top spike, cream horns, big ginger beard with moustache, small peach face, brown armor tunic with skirt, dark belt with gold buckle (#f1b434 sampled from dwarf.png), grey mail pauldron on his left and a brown one on his right, leather bracers, dark trousers and boots, and the single-bit axe from dwarfAxe.png (steel head, brown haft) held upright in his right hand (screen-left in the down view)",
   "attack": "7-frame two-handed overhead chop: 0 raise, 1 wind up with the axe behind his back (lifted onto the toes), 2 swing over, 3 chop into a forward crouch (HIT), 4 hold the impact, 5 recover, 6 settle",
   "weak": "- The consistency check reports walk_left/right sway as 1.0px (rule: >=2px). In the side views his side-to-side sway goes toward and away from the camera, so it cannot appear on screen. Bob there is 5-8px and frames 0 and 4 differ by about 800px, so the walk still reads.\n- His left hand does not exactly grip the haft during the chop (both arms follow the same arc, so the hands are near the haft but not locked to it).\n- In the down/up views the chop points toward or away from the camera, so impact frames 3 and 4 show a short axe beside the body. The side views are the strong ones.\n- The blade is flat to the camera in the down view, so in the side views it is an edge-on silver sliver.\n- His face is only a few px between the helm and the beard (as in the reference). The eyes are 1-2px dark dots.\n- Attack frames are 96x96 but walk/idle/hurt are 64x80, so the attack sheet needs its own origin (0.9271 vs 0.9125). See the table."
  }
